Subject: [PATCH] receipts: the export branch's series check PASSES - both
 halves, rc=0

602 patches byte-identical to a fresh generation AND to a committed blob; replayed cleanly onto the re-keyed base 4627f376f; replayed tree IDENTICAL to export outside patches/series. Export tip cb4df7a48.

Recorded honestly: it failed on the first attempt for two reasons, both mine and neither a defect in the rewrite - the fork's own convergence rule (committing the series creates a commit the series cannot yet contain, which is why main takes the same two steps every regen), and a directory pathspec that stages tracked changes and deletions but not newly generated files, leaving 20 regenerated patches untracked.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - an evidence document; no code path is touched.
---
 RELEASE-PREP-PHASE2-RECEIPTS.md | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

